        <p>JAMESON'S RIDE.</p>
        <p>Authentic records of this Historical Event now reach England, and the Crisis is virtually over. Peace and plenty again rule through tha Golden Territory of the llransvaal, and the act of Dr. Jameson links this modern Hero inalienably to one of the Historic Incidents of the Century. No infringement of our neutrality can be urged against us in laying bare to the Liverpool public a guinea of strong local interest and advantage. A rumour was current previously, but is only con- firmed with" Dr. Jim's' arrival, that his brave band of Volunteers had become possessed (prior to the Raid) of the redoubtable clothing manufactured especially for South Africa by Messrs. HENOCHS- BERG &amp; ELLIS, UNIVERSITY HOUSE, Islington, Liverpool, and that the Natural Wool Under- wear famous .for sub climates shipped to the South African Repuplic, as well as to the Char- tered Company's Territory, by Messrs. HENOCHS- BERG &amp; ELLIS, was worn by the Doctor's helps BsuoduringTsBa, their 1 Ire sTxotsesre. try, tftstoegsr time. The Government Serges (Passing full test for shades, dyes, and strength) are kept in stock at University House. Messrs. HE.NOCHSBERG .5t ELLIS are prepared to under- takeffßoroDumETßHtShs forse GENTLEMEN'SaIeTts m 3 sast.e,raianlsc] forof which they now hold a good selection, as the contract for the Natal Government is in course of completion by this well-known firm.</p>
      </div>
