      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0075" n="art0075">
        <head>"THE PANTHEON." GAYTHORN, MANCHESTER.</head>
        <p>"THE PANTHEON." GAYTHORN, MANCHESTER.</p>
        <p>NVEEKLY CHAT:— Worsley's despatch goods to all parts of the world, and believe in advertising as one of the essentials of success. No firm in Manchester has shown more spirit and enterprise In advertising, the turnover has increased enormously. the output at the present time is the largest in Manchester. ' The main secret of success is small profits, combined with the largest stock hi England to select from. A visit to' The Pantheon " is both instructive and interesting ; it contains over a million square feet of showrooms, is fitted throughout with the electric light, a new showroom, storerooms, carpet factory, and an entirely new pianoforte saloon forming the latest additions to the premises. The Manchester Electric Company have all but completed the new electric installation 'frith powerful engines and dynamo. Pay a visit to '• The Pantheon" before selecting your furniture, it will cost you nothing, but may profit you muc'. ; you are at perfect liberty to inspect without being expected to purchase.</p>
        <p>ALL the goods advertised are for cash, but may be had on the deferred payment system if required, with- out any addition to the cost. Insp etion invited.</p>
        <p>READ ON OF BARGAINS GREAT AND WONDERFUL. EPITOME OF BARGAINS IN HOUSES OF FURNITURE. For £l5; usual price, £2O. A smart House of Furniture, con- sisting of the whole of the Furnitere for 3 Rooms, the Sitting-room having Solid Mahogany or Walnut Furni- ture; the Bedroom containing a Bedroom Suite corn plete ; also Solid Brass and Enamel Bedstead, complete with all the Bedding. &amp;c. The Kitchen is also fur- nished complete, besides Hall, Stairs, Landing, and Scullery. Everything is as good as new, and cost over £4O not six months ago. A full detailed list will be sent post free on applLation. For £25; usual price, £35. A magnificent House of Furni- ture, removed from Sale, cut £7O, for 4 Rooms. Par- ticular. on application. For £4O, cost £95. A grand House of Furniture, mostly made by Ogden, in splendid :tondition, equal to new; one of the gems; the best bargain ever offered by Worsley's. Contains furnitur- for dining-room, draw- ing-room, and three bedrooms, besides kitchen; the sundries are worth £lO. Suites t every room. The furniture can be guiranteed throughout, being all solid and well made. Send for full detailed list. For £6O. Complete House of Furniture. This lot is a defaulter's house of furniture which we supplied on th deferred payment system, but which contract was never completed. It was a bargain in the first instance, but is doubly so now. The dilling-rostm is furnished en- tirely in solid brown oak, the drawing-room is Chip- pendale mahogany, the best bedroom in solid walnut and burr, the visitors' bedroom in satinwood. The kitchen servants' bedrooms are nicely furnished, and besides there are the pictures, curtains, blinds. sun- dries, &amp;c., also the best carpets and oilcloths through out. The whole lot for £6O; cheap at £l2O. Send a once for a complete detailed Ist of this lot to Worsley's For 100 Guineas. The Best Complete House of Furniture i Manchester for this price, or even double this price. Worsley's in this lot offer all the heavy. substantial furniture, removed horn Brooklands, for the 100 guineas, and will undertake to sup ly new carpets and linoleum throughout without making any additional charge for this lot, The turniture is worth double the amount, still, whoever buys this lot may have perfont freedom in selection of carpets and linoleum. The furniture is for dining, dtawing, sitting, and three bedrooms. Send for the complete list, when you can better judge of the most extraordinary bargain eve offered.</p>
        <p>The above form the 18t Division of the Flying Squadron oi wonderful bargains mobilised at •• The Pantheon."</p>
        <p>GREAT BARGAINS IN DINING - ROOM</p>
        <p>FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>For £2O. The Best Solid Oak Dining-room Suite ever offered for this money, containing suite of nine pieces—couch' two easy chairs, and six easy chairs, in morocco. A magnificent sideboard, dining-table, and overmantle, all in solid brown oak, exquts tely carved in bast relief. The lot is worth £5O. Inspection invited. Will be bent on approval anywhere. For £lO 10. A Complete Dining-room Suite. Sideboard Dining Table, and Overmantel in Walnut, similar t the one £2O. The whole lot for £lO 10s„ not 10 guineas each, but the lot for that price. Call and see' this lot for yourself, it will almost knock you down with surprise, being simply given away. Five years warranty. Money returned if not approved. For £45. Very Handsome Dining-rot-1n Furniture in Pollard oak and moroccs.,. Six feet Sideb,ard with fine hand- some massive back, beautifully fitted w.th exquisitely shaped bevelled crystal mirrors; magnificent Couch, Two fine Easy Chairs. and Six standard padded back Single Chairs. splendid Pollard oak Dining Table, with fire ie,ves and leaf case; and last a capital Overmantel, with d mble bevels. The sideboard cost more money than wa want for the lot. Inspect at WORSLEY'S Hundreds of lots at all sorts of prices, from £lO to £250 Dining-room Suites from £3 10s. to £75. On View.</p>
        <p>DRAWING-ROOM FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>For £lO 10s. Avery pretty Drawing-room Suite of seven " pieces in slik tapestry. and Ca'sinet complete. very nicely made. second-hand. not much soiled, presents a very nice appearance, and a won,lerful bargain. For £2O. A good substantial Drawing-room Suite, rather old-fashioned, but delightfully comfortable, upholstered In old Gobelin Tapestry, winderfully clean for its age. Upholstered in the best possible manner for its age. All the framework is as good as the day it was made, in fact. furniture is not made now as good at, when this suite was manufactured. Consists of Settee, Two Sutherland Easy Chairs, and Six Single Chairs, Cabinet, and Overmantel A rare bargain. For £35. A rich recherche Drawing-room Suite, in carved Chippendale, covered in exquisite Genoa velvet, with raised flowers ; the framework is exquisitely carved. suite of seven pieces, also Two extra Occasional Chairs and a fine Cubinet of original des go, Overmantel, Two Who Tables, and Coal Cabinet. A rare Bargain at £35; Hundreds of Suites from £4 to £BO. Cabinets from 50s. to £65. Overmantels from 15s. to £25. Thousands of link-</p>
        <p>BEDROOM FURNITURE BARGAINS.</p>
        <p>W. H.</p>
        <p>GAYTHORN, MANCHESTER, CLOSE TO CENTRAL STATION. HOURS OF BUSINESS, 9 TO 7 EVERY DAY.</p>
        <p>For £7 10e. A Capital 31t. 61n. American Walnut Bedroom Sultemithenclosed stands. pedestAl chairs,and rail com- plete. A downeght good, substantial bedroom suite, quite as good as any new one,and in splendid condition. A Bargain. For £lO. A very similar Suite,but 4ft. widedn Satinwood.for £lO, cost £25 when new ; has been entirely repolished and renovated ; equal to new; guaranteed for ten years ; well worth I' now. For £l5. A Massive &amp;did Iseown Oak Bedroom Suite, sft. wide, the wardrobe being in two parts, one long cen- tre door fitted with plate glass. the panels of the end doors are heavily carved in bee relief; both washstand and dressing table we fully enclosed; three chairs, vedeital, and towel horse cnmplete. A fine, massive, handsome suite Inspect early, as it is bound to go quickly. Worsley's. For £2l. A Magnificent 6ft. Bedroom Suite, solid through- out, in exquisitely fi 'tired wood, cost £6O when new ; 4ft. pedestal dressing table and washstand.tab'e. de nuit,and three chairs. The wardrobe is very hand- some, being a fine gold design, proi4,cting centre door. The suite is cheap at £5O to-day, and is a great bargain. Woraley'e. Hundreds of Bedroom Suites from 355. to £l5O. andrecis of Wardrobes from 355. to £25. Hundreds of Pairs of Stands from 10s. 6i. to £25. BEDSTEAD BARGAINS.</p>
        <p>For £5. A Magnifilent Solid Brass Bedstead, cost £2O, with spring mattress and wool overlay complete. A won .ier- mul bargain. For £2 10s. A Brass Bedstead -nd Spring Mattress, together with wool overlay and bolster and two piliows, cost £l2. For RI 15s. A God Brass and Enamelled Bedstead, Spring Mattress, and Wool Overlay.</p>
        <p>A Capital Lot of Blt DSTB AD 4. slightly soiled, being cleared during our Big Sale at ss. to 10s. each; 5,000 Bedsteads in stock from 4s. to £2B each. All stile% Spring Mattresses and Bedding being cleared out at any price.</p>
        <p>SITTING-ROOM FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>In this department an immense clearance must be effected. We have an enormous lot of odd lots here, such a. odd Couches, Sofas, Chairs, Cheffoniers, Bookeases. Tables. Dressers, itc., which we propose to mark down, and offer at startling prices. We briefly enumer.te a few :—Hair Cloth Couch, in mahogany. 215., cost £4; Splendid Sofa, 253. A fine lot of chairs. all mahvany, at ss. each, some worth 203. each. Mahogany Cheffonier, 355. ; with plate glass back,4sB. Several old-fashioned Dining t ables from 103. to 203. Loo Table, in mahogany, cost £lO, for 208. Several Spanish Mahogany Carved Back Dressers, worth £lO to £l2 each, for £4, £5 and 26. Full-sized Painted Dressers, with sycamore tops, 7 drawers and clipboards, for 203. to 355. Kitchen Chairs Is. each. Bedroom Chairs. Is. 3t each. Chest of Drawers, 10s. to 20s. each. Thousands of odd articles to clear at any price.</p>
        <p>OFFICE FURNITURE.</p>
        <p>We have several job lots of Office Furniture to clear, also several Second hand American Desks, Cylinders, Vat-tops, Registered. &amp;c. Flat-tops 108. 0504. each. Cylinder Desks, £4 to £8 103. AMeriCan Desl;s, £6 to £l2 meta. Chairs. Pigeon-boles. Bookcases, and Cupboards equally cheap: A rare opportunity for picking up something cheap and good.</p>
        <p>WORSLEY, THE PANTHEON,</p>
      </div>
