        <p>RUNCORN UNION. —CONTRACTS for PROVI- SIONS and SUPPLIIIi for the Half-year ending October 3rd, 1896. The GUARDIANS of the POOR of the RUNCORN UNION are desirous of receiving TENDERS from parties willing to Contract for the supply of New Milk, Buttermilk, Fresh Butter and Fresh Eggs (for twelve months), Flour, Oatmeal, Groceries, Peas, Cheese. Salt Butter ; Cod Liver and Paraffin Oil ; Quinine ; good Beef to consist of vein plec.s intact and fiat Ribs with B.me ; one Round weekly not to exceed 2515. and 50.bs. per week of the best Butcher's Meat for the Officers, and Sides of Mutton ; Bread ; Home-Cure'! Bacon ; Potatoes' Wheat Straw; Drapery and C'otiaing ; Men's, Women's, Bays' and Girls' Shoes of v.rions sizes, as per samples, to be seen at the Workhouse, Dutton, and Shoe Mending; House Coal (Colliers. to be named) ; gocd Deal Coffins, specifying size and including plate with name, age, and date of death,to be delivered in the Union when and where required; Coke; Crting at per mile, Funerals at per Funeral. PArties tendPring for the supply of the above-mentioned Goods, will be required to d-liver the stme at the Workhouse, free of cost to the Guardians, how and when required. Tenders to be accompanied with Samples (except Drapery Goods), as far as practicable. Th. Guardians do not bind themselves to accept the i owest or any Tender. Persons desirous of Tendering must apply by letter to my °Mc- in Runcorn, for a printed Form of Tender (and none other can be entertained), where a Schedule of the various articles required and further particulars may be obtnined. Sealed Tenders addressed to the Guardians, to be for- warded to the Clerk's. Offi,e, Runcorn, on or before Monday, the 16th day of March. 1896. endorsel "Tender for" The Teneers will be opened and considered at a Meeting of the Guardians to be held in the Boardroom, Dutton, on the, 17th day of March, 1896, at 12-30 p m. parties whose Tenders are accepted must enter into written Contr set, and be prepared to enter into a Bond with two sureties, if require i by the Guardians. By order of the Board. JOHN ASH fON, Clerk to the Guardians.</p>
