      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-03-07_WidnesExaminer_art0092" n="art0092">
        <head>MAKE LIFE ENJOYABLE.</head>
        <p>MAKE LIFE ENJOYABLE.</p>
        <p>Loss of health means loss of all which makes life en- joySble ; for, in addition to the bodily pain and suffering which it cause:, it entails a vast amount of mental pain and anxiety, especially in the homes of the working classes, It brings in its train a host of discomforts which retard the recovery of the sufferer, and hinder, instead of assisting, Nature to perform her functions. When a working man suffers from any ailment which prevents his following his daily avocation, he is natur- ally filled with anxiety regarding the maintenance of those depending on him for their daily sustenance. His very love for his family retards and hinders his speedy recovery, and his spirits become depresf ed at the antici- pation of the gloomy prospects before them in the event of a long continuance of his illness. It is well known that depression of spirits often proves a serious bar to a speedy recovery. These results arise in addition to the various incon- veniences and discomforts which the sufferer and his family experience as direct results of his illness, such as additional expenses for luxuries for the sick, with in- creased difficulty to obtain those luxuries, or even the necessities of life.</p>
        <p>Most of the various forms of disease which trouble the labouring classes of the country, and which are often attributable, more or less, to some unhealthly condition of their daily work, may be. classed under a few leading beads.</p>
        <p>To avoid th 9 discomforts arising from various forms of disease,every working man should seek the aid of</p>
